rowing his company  Chandler understood the importance of  not messing with perfection as an  increasing number of copycat beverages  found their way into the market Kaler  might have changed the shape of his  bottle or altered his marketing message  but he never once made the crucial error  that his later successes would after  creating the perfect drink he never  again changed its secret recipe  Chandler knew that an increase in  competitive industry it was important to  stand out and to keep his customers on  their toes but he did not dare mess with  what he saw as excellence  after all it was not broke why fix it  however coca-cola executives tried to  replace the old with the new  as a result of launching new coke the  company's market share tanked candle was  proven right again changes sometimes bad  especially when you try and change the  perfect drink according the canler you  can change the marketing but never  change the drink  keeping the coca-cola recipe secret  meant it would always be unique ASA  canler was a strong business person and  aggressive when it came to all of his  ventures but he believed personal wealth  should benefit the community unheard of  in his day he would challenge other  wealthy business people to match  everything he gave to charity  a lot of his money went towards the  building of wesley Memorial Hospital  which is now known as Emory University  Hospital Candler did a lot for education  and is considered the founder of Emory  University according to one story he  would not associate with other  businesspeople that did not share his  point of view about giving back to the  community the feeling was proven in  public when he slapped one of the  richest men in Atlanta at the time for  not giving money to help expand Emory  University this story ran in all the  local newspapers and was front-page news  for more than a week until the wealthy  businessperson finally gave 12,500 to  the University and did it publicly  thank you for joi